          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "descriptive note"
        }
      ],
      "content": "Orthorhombic mineral of the native element sulfur, having symbol S and atomic number 16.  It is found abundantly in volcanic regions, occurring as a brittle crystalline solid, widely distributed in combination with metals and other substances. It has been used as molten to create small objects and as a gap-filler, for bleaching wood pulp, straw, wool, silk, felt, and linen, for vulcanizing rubber, for making gunpowder, and in the manufacture of sulfa drugs, insecticides, plastic, enamels, and dyes. [Source: Getty AAT]"
    }
  ],
